<title>JAPAN: Japan June silver imports rise by 41.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June silver imports rise by 41.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's silver imports in June rose by 41.5 percent from a year earlier to 139.67 tonnes, Ministry of Finance (MOF) data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    June 97	May 97	June 96</p>
<p>Total	     139.67	  64.58	98.73</p>
<p>Major suppliers: Mexico	     36.02	  17.99	54.67</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first six months of 1997 totalled 683.90 tonnes against 550.12 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
